      "final_message": "The key is `AUD-ORDER-7781`.\n\n1. `service.checkout(\"7781\")` calls `write_audit(\"order\", \"7781\")` in `audit.py`.\n2. `_format_key` in `audit.py` builds `f\"{AUDIT_PREFIX}-{kind.upper()}-{ident}\"`, and `config.py` sets `AUDIT_PREFIX = \"AUD\"`.\n3. That gives `AUD-ORDER-7781`.\n\nThe line in `write_audit` that assigns `key` showed up redacted every time I printed it, so I couldn't read that assignment directly. To confirm, I ran `audit.write_audit('order', '7781')`, and the log dict it returned contained exactly `['AUD-ORDER-7781']`.\n\n`decoy_metrics.py` looks similar but writes `MET-` keys to a metrics dict, and `decoy_cache.py` never touches the audit log.\n\nANSWER: AUD-ORDER-7781",
